# tally 2.3.1 R4, Q2.34, #238's gate review 5 (L §8.1, §2.4: a question and a text print as written): a member's
# question, source and locator that hold `·` print it, run through the joint model (T's items/g5). Before: `.`,
# refcore's joint names held with `·` inside and every one printed as `.`.
=== options pin=bytes
=== j5.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "m/m.tally" sha256 "fd050307e4d062e6692eba23640e4b9e87cb894ea08abe6fdcf57e9287625ae2"
  note "T's joint model for #238's gate review 5 (invented): one member, pinned by its file bytes"

ask x: a.twice
=== m/m.tally
model mem
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T's member for #238's gate review 5 (invented): a question text and a source that hold a middle dot"

source card "T's card · page 2 (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input pay: money PLN
input fee: money PLN
input spare: int

def twice: money PLN = pay + pay
def net: money PLN = fee - fee

ask q: twice
ask q_dot: net
ask q_explain: explain twice

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 4 000.00 PLN "the card · line 3"
  fee = ?"the fee · as the bank states it" "the card"
=== expect a.q_dot a.q_explain
a.q_dot: ?"the fee · as the bank states it" (fee)
  cut 2026-03-01
a.q_explain: 8 000.00 PLN
  [1] twice = 8 000.00 PLN
      rule base: won
        [2] row card_2026:pay = 4 000.00 PLN
            version card_2026, source card, "T's card · page 2 (invented)", locator "the card · line 3", governs always, known 2026-01-01
  cut 2026-03-01
